[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) merged 412 reports and was marked known: one cause, the shared
parser, fix queued. [CauseTable](/kb/incidents/4471) already shows a second cause, `hint`,
living in the same ticket with no ticket of its own. Checking the 412 reports' own text against
that split — not against either cause's definition — turns up a third: 5 reports that describe
a plain one-day difference, which a day/month swap can never produce.

<Callout kind="warn">
Three problems were merged into one ticket because [decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)
merges on subject line. "Wrong day on the invite" and "Date is wrong" describe three different
bugs that all produce the same sentence.
</Callout>

## The real split

<ThreeCauseTable ticket={4471} />

## Where each one went

- **parser** (374) — the parser fix already queued against #4471. Filed as its own issue:
  [kcprnoj/support-kb-4471#1](https://github.com/kcprnoj/support-kb-4471/issues/1).
- **hint** (33) — booking-v3's date hint mismatches day-first tenants on the `form` channel.
  Unticketed before now: [kcprnoj/support-kb-4471#2](https://github.com/kcprnoj/support-kb-4471/issues/2).
- **drift** (5) — a one-day difference, not a swap. The desk's own `oneDayMove` note in
  `desk-notes.json` already named these 5 reports; nobody gave them a ticket.
  [kcprnoj/support-kb-4471#3](https://github.com/kcprnoj/support-kb-4471/issues/3).

## Lessons

- Dedupe by subject merges by what a report *sounds like*, not by what caused it. Two bugs with
  the same symptom will share a ticket until someone checks the cause, not just the count.
- A desk note that says "these read differently" and files them anyway is a problem waiting for
  a ticket, not a resolved footnote.
- 374 + 33 + 5 = 412. The original ticket's count was right; its one-cause story wasn't.

